---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Background"
  description="Senior Frontend Engineer and UI Architect with 15+ years of experience across enterprise web architecture, frontend platforms, and applied AI systems."
  schemaType="person"
  wide
>
  <header class="border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="site-shell grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-end">
      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <p class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--accent)]">Biography & Perspective</p>
        <h1 class="font-display mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.06] tracking-[-0.04em] text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-6xl">Orielsy Diaz</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="max-w-md text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] sm:text-[15px] lg:col-span-4">
        Senior Frontend Engineer and UI Architect with 15+ years of experience building scalable web applications, enterprise platforms, and high-profile digital experiences.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="site-shell">
    <section class="grid gap-8 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <h2 class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Core Background & Positioning</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose max-w-none lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          My deepest professional background is frontend engineering and UI architecture: building enterprise applications, establishing reusable component and frontend patterns, modernizing long-lived platforms, and turning complex automation and backend functionality into interfaces people can actually use.
        </p>
        <p>
          More recently, I have designed and built repository-specific coding-agent knowledge systems and prototyped an MCP Apps MVP, while evaluating local-model runtimes such as WebLLM and Ollama. Together, these efforts extend my frontend and UI architecture background into <strong>applied AI, context engineering, and developer tools</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm particularly interested in the application layer of AI: how agents, context, tools, and interfaces come together to create useful products and developer experiences.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <h2 class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">How I Think</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="border-y border-[var(--border-subtle)] lg:col-span-8">
        <li class="grid gap-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-6 sm:grid-cols-[52px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-6">
          <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">The Right Context at the Right Time</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">More information is not automatically better. Whether the consumer is an autonomous coding agent or a person navigating a complex product, I tend to think in terms of filtering and surfacing the information or capability useful at that particular moment rather than presenting everything at once.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-4 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-6 sm:grid-cols-[52px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-6">
          <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">AI as a Capability, Not Just a Chatbot</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Chat is only one narrow modality. Structured extraction, inline classification, semantic filtering, contextual actions, and adaptive guidance can become ordinary capabilities inside interface architecture without forcing users into a conversational text box.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="grid gap-4 py-6 sm:grid-cols-[52px_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-6">
          <span class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] text-[var(--accent)]">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)]">Abstraction Should Remove Complexity, Not Relocate It</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Some of the most rewarding interface problems involve taking complicated underlying automation, backend mechanics, or technical systems and designing an interaction model that makes the capability substantially easier for a person to understand and control.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <h2 class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Career & Service</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose max-w-none lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          Throughout my career, I have led frontend and UI technical direction, established engineering standards, collaborated closely across design and engineering teams, and remained hands-on in the codebase.
        </p>
        <p>
          I served four years in the U.S. Navy from 2002 to 2006 as a Petty Officer (SH3). While serving, I independently designed and developed my ship's website outside my assigned duties, work that was recognized with a Navy Commendation Medal.
        </p>
        <p>
          After leaving the Navy, I studied Computer Science at William Paterson University and worked part-time as a web developer before moving into frontend engineering full-time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] py-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <h2 class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Creative & Adjacent Interests</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose max-w-none lg:col-span-8">
        <p>
          Outside of software, I'm especially interested in modular synthesis, gaming, and the places where physical and digital interfaces meet. MIDI, control surfaces, signal routing, and interactive systems are areas I find myself naturally drawn toward.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-3">
        <h2 class="font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--text-muted)]">Connect & Channels</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-4 font-editorial-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] lg:col-span-8">
        <a href="https://github.com/orielsy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:text-[var(--accent)]">GitHub (@orielsy) <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/orielsy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:text-[var(--accent)]">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/rss.xml" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:text-[var(--accent)]">Subscribe via RSS <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
